06:04.660 --> 06:10.070
But in order to understand the results let's go and include the product ID in the results.

06:10.070 --> 06:12.190
So product ID and execute.

06:12.190 --> 06:17.030
So now by looking to the results you can see that the data is divided into four windows.

06:17.190 --> 06:17.870
Let's see them.

06:17.870 --> 06:19.510
It's going to be by the product ID.

06:19.750 --> 06:22.550
So this dimension going to be controlling the partition.

06:22.550 --> 06:25.670
So the first window going to be the product ID 101.

06:25.670 --> 06:28.750
So we have the total sales for this product 140.

06:28.790 --> 06:31.230
And the next window going to be 102.

06:31.270 --> 06:32.830
The third one 104.

06:32.950 --> 06:38.350
And the last window, it's going to be only one row the 105 and the total sales with 60.

06:38.350 --> 06:39.830
So with that we have solved the task.

06:39.830 --> 06:42.430
We have the total sales for each product.

06:42.430 --> 06:43.910
And as well we have some details.

06:43.990 --> 06:47.390
Now I would like to show you the dynamic of the window function.

06:47.390 --> 06:50.910
We can add multiple aggregations on multiple levels.

06:50.910 --> 06:51.830
Let me show you what I mean.

06:51.830 --> 06:57.230
Let's say we stay with the same example, but we're going to find the total sales across all orders

06:57.230 --> 07:00.670
and as well the total sales for each products.

07:00.670 --> 07:06.510
So what we can do, we can do the window functions on different levels by for example here removing

07:06.510 --> 07:07.430
the whole definition.

07:07.430 --> 07:12.400
So here we have the total sales for the entire data for the first task, and the next one going to be

07:12.400 --> 07:15.160
the total sales but divided by the product ID.

07:15.200 --> 07:17.680
Let's rename it by products.

07:18.600 --> 07:20.560
Let's go and execute this.

07:20.600 --> 07:21.360
And now you know what.

07:21.360 --> 07:26.080
I'm going to go and add the sales as well just to explain the flexibility of the window function.

07:26.080 --> 07:28.920
So let's go add the sales and execute it again.

07:28.960 --> 07:34.560
And now by looking to the results you can see we have the sales informations three times but with different

07:34.560 --> 07:39.160
granularities the first sales, the sales itself without any aggregations.

07:39.440 --> 07:42.200
It is the highest level of details of the sales.

07:42.200 --> 07:47.160
And we're going to have the sales for each order, the next one, the total sales with the window function.

07:47.200 --> 07:49.320
Here we have the highest level of aggregations.

07:49.320 --> 07:52.200
So we have the total sales of all orders.

07:52.200 --> 07:54.080
And the last one the total sales by product.

07:54.080 --> 07:57.520
It's something like in the middle we are aggregating on a window.

07:57.720 --> 07:59.640
And the window is going to be the product ID.

07:59.640 --> 08:03.080
So as you can see we have different granularities of the aggregations.

08:03.080 --> 08:06.760
And this is exactly the flexibility that we have with the window function.

08:06.760 --> 08:09.170
We can do all those stuff in one query.

08:09.210 --> 08:11.930
Okay, so now let's keep moving and adding stuff to our task.

08:11.970 --> 08:17.490
It's going to say find the total sales for each combination of the products and the order status.

08:17.690 --> 08:23.770
So this time we have to divide the data not only by the product but as well with another dimension the

08:23.770 --> 08:24.650
order status.

08:24.850 --> 08:26.410
So now let's see how we can do that.

08:26.410 --> 08:29.730
I'm going to just show the dimension order status in the results.

08:30.570 --> 08:33.250
And we're going to add the following thing.

08:33.610 --> 08:37.930
So some sales over since it's a window function.

08:37.930 --> 08:41.050
And let's go now and define the window partition by.

08:41.090 --> 08:46.930
So we have again the product ID but not only this dimension as well the order status.

08:47.170 --> 08:52.170
And let's go and call it sales by products and status.

08:52.210 --> 08:53.890
Let me just rename those stuff.

08:53.930 --> 08:54.490
Okay.

08:54.690 --> 08:56.490
So let's go and execute.

08:56.530 --> 08:56.810
All right.

08:56.810 --> 08:58.130
So now let's check the results.

08:58.130 --> 08:59.930
It is the last aggregation over here.

08:59.930 --> 09:04.770
